# L §8.5 (tally 2.1.1): "A run's warnings print sorted by code, then by their text, compared by code point, whatever
# the order of the reality's files." The files are given z.tally first: WARN-NEGATIVE (konto: 2 500.00 less 1 000.00
# on each 5th, below zero from 2026-03-05) sorts before WARN-UNREAD, and the unread items sort by their text, def aa,
# def zz, input bb, wherever they are declared and in whatever order load finds them (issue #13, T1's gap I-5).
=== z.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "plan"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input save_amt: money PLN
input save_dom: int
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place savings: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
def zz: int = 0

move save[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, save_dom)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to savings amount save_amt

version plan_2026
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  save_amt = 1 000.00 PLN "own"
  save_dom = 5 "own"
  opening[konto] = 2 500.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "statement"
  opening[savings] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "statement"

ask k: bal(konto, 2026-03-31), bal(savings, 2026-03-31)
=== a.tally
part extra
  tally 2

def aa: int = 1
input bb: int
=== expect
k: (-500.00 PLN, 3 000.00 PLN)
...
warning: WARN-NEGATIVE konto is below zero from 2026-03-05
warning: WARN-UNREAD def aa is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD def zz is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input bb is read by nothing
